      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1859 Van Buren became part of newly created Carter County and was chosen as its county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Buren%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first bridge over the Current River at Van Buren was a suspension bridge built in 1893–94 for $4,500.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
